docs: one manual with a guide and a reference under it (#190)

The guide and the reference were two separate Scribble documents, two
entries in info.rkt. Every link between them therefore went through
Racket's local-redirect indirection, which is rewritten by a script
loaded over file:// -- so served over HTTP every @racket[tensor] in the
guide landed on a "Redirections" placeholder rather than its entry.

Restructured after rkt-polars, which does not have the problem: one
document, torch.scrbl, carrying the module's overview and
@defmodule[torch], with guide.scrbl and reference.scrbl as parts beneath
it and a shared table of contents. Links between the halves are now
ordinary relative links, and only links into Racket's own manuals still
need --redirect-main when rendering a copy to serve.

@defmodule[torch] moves here from shape.scrbl, so @racketmodname[torch]
no longer resolves to the 29-line "Transpose shorthand" chapter.

